<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gjon Kastrioti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1437</span> · Also known as John Castriot</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gjon Kastrioti was an Albanian lord who built a principality in the Mat valley and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diber">Dibër</a> region, reaching towards the Adriatic near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lezhe">Lezhë</a>. He accepted Ottoman overlordship while trading with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and Ragusa, and sent his sons as hostages to the Ottoman court. One of them was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Gjergj Kastrioti</a>, known as Skanderbeg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gjon-kastrioti.jpg" alt="Gjon Kastrioti" width="192" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GjonKastrioti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
